[Music]  street art is everywhere it's global  but street art is very different in very  different cities  [Music]  we know new york you know paris but i  want people to know singapore street art  my name is zul commonly known as zero  and i am a street artist  [Music]  singapore is known for its greenery and  its order  the rebellious nature of street art does  not fit in the bigger construct of  singapore but i think that's what makes  it interesting  i've been in public spaces where the  works are accessible to everyone  what i do is always free for people they  see an artwork in a space that they  never expect to be i think that's the  beauty of it  once it's completed it belongs to the  public space so it gets removed in an  hour it's fine it's meant to be  temporary  singapore is a small country everything  changes very quickly and street art  reflects that very well  i first got involved in street art right  after my military service in my early  20s  i was skateboarding it was kind of like  a natural progression for me to move  from one part of street culture into  another  when i just started out making art on  the streets i was more concerned about  just the process of painting  now doing this for 15 years i'm thinking  about the process of storytelling and  what i want to express as an artist  mostly i'm interested in expressing the  human condition especially in urban  society because that's where i'm from  that's how i was raised and that's where  i get ideas from  in 2013 i was awarded the young artist  award by the national arts council which  is a first for a street artist it's one  of the highlights of my career because  i'm representing a community of artists  that's always on the  fringe being more in public like gives  me more motivation to make better works  and advocate as to what street art is  especially in the context of singapore  to create new things is to break all  things and remake it  innovation is disruption  [Music]  you

